tern-cv:56195246-ec5d-4050-a1c6-af786fbec715 prez:label "scientific name"@en ;
	prez:description "The formal biological name, with authorship and date information, if known. When forming part of an identification, this should be the name in lowest level taxonomic rank that can be determined." , "A scientific name is a formal, standardized biological name given to an organism of interest and may represent a taxonomic rank (e.g., family, genus, species, etc.). The names are usually compliant with the most recent nomenclature codes. This is not to be confused with 'taxon', which represents a group of organisms listed under hierarchical taxonomic ranks." .
